Package: circuitscaper
Title: Circuit-Theory Connectivity with 'Circuitscape', 'Omniscape' and Dipole Methods
Version: 0.2.0.9000
Authors@R: person("Matthew", "Kling", email = "mattkling@berkeley.edu",
                  role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Author: Matthew Kling [aut, cre, cph]
Maintainer: Matthew Kling <mattkling@berkeley.edu>
Description: Landscape connectivity modeling with circuit theory. Users
    work entirely in R with familiar objects (SpatRaster, file paths) while
    'Julia' handles computation invisibly. Runs all four 'Circuitscape' modes
    (pairwise, one-to-all, all-to-one, advanced) and 'Omniscape'
    moving-window analysis through the 'Circuitscape.jl' and 'Omniscape.jl'
    'Julia' packages; these methods are described in McRae (2006)
    <doi:10.1111/j.0014-3820.2006.tb00500.x> and Landau et al. (2021)
    <doi:10.21105/joss.02829>. Also provides experimental dipole methods,
    which map pairwise, omnidirectional and cross-era connectivity from
    random source-sink pairs superposed on a single factored circuit, at a
    cost that doesn't grow with the number of pairs.
